@startuml
title Gestion des quotas - Scenario de scale

participant Admin
participant Deployment
participant "Admission\nController" as admission
database "ResourceQuota\n4 pods max" as quota

== Etat initial: 2 replicas ==
Admin -> Deployment : 2 replicas demandes
Deployment -> admission : Create pod1
admission -> quota : Check quota
quota --> admission : 1/4 pods OK
admission --> Deployment : pod1 APPROVED

Deployment -> admission : Create pod2
admission -> quota : Check quota
quota --> admission : 2/4 pods OK
admission --> Deployment : pod2 APPROVED

note right
  Etat: 2 pods Running
end note

== Tentative de scale a 10 replicas ==
Admin -> Deployment : kubectl scale --replicas=10
note right: Demande 8 pods supplementaires

Deployment -> admission : Create pod3
admission -> quota : Check quota (3/4)
admission --> Deployment : pod3 APPROVED

Deployment -> admission : Create pod4
admission -> quota : Check quota (4/4)
admission --> Deployment : pod4 APPROVED

Deployment -> admission : Create pod5
admission -> quota : Check quota (5/4)
quota --> admission : QUOTA EXCEEDED
admission -[#red]-> Deployment : pod5 REJECTED

Deployment -> admission : Create pod6
admission -> quota : Check quota (still 5/4)
admission -[#red]-> Deployment : pod6-10 REJECTED

note right
  Etat final: 4 pods Running
  Events: "exceeded quota"
end note

Admin -> Deployment : Get status
Deployment --> Admin : spec.replicas=10\nstatus.replicas=4

@enduml
